    "description": "• Original engineer designing and deploying PromoteIQ’s ad server and associated delivery systems (written in Java, Python, and some C++).\n\t◦ Led the delivery team’s effort to refactor the ad server to better prepare for an ever-increasing amount of business and performance requirements.\n\t◦ Worked very closely with Product to design and implement new features for the ad server. This involved individual efforts early on as the sole delivery engineer, to leading team projects as the team expanded.\n\t◦ Coordinated with the data team to determine downstream data processing requirements.\n\t◦ Spent significant amounts of time profiling our ad servers, using JProfiler, to weed out inefficiencies and locate areas of improvement. These optimizations greatly impacted performance and revenue.\n\t◦ Built and maintained the ad servers’ store of budget and pacing data globally using Aerospike.\n\t\t▪ Made countless improvements on how event metrics were stored, structured and retrieved, given a very high demand from the ad servers.\n\t\t▪ Later on guided a separate team in the effort to migrate this data to Azure/CosmosDB later within Microsoft. This involved members of our team and Microsoft’s CosmosDB team.\n• Rebuilt the early data serialization service using Protocol buffers.\n• Built the product catalog caching service for the ad server to provide a greater amount of metadata for the ad servers’ decisioning engine. Products were in the millions per retailer and provided great storage and memory needs.\n• Built an additional service on top of the ad server to serve promoted products through emails.\n• Developed V1 of the sales attribution system, which processes the retailers’ checkout sales in real-time and attributes product purchases to Impressions/Click events delivered by PromoteIQ. (ROAS/ROI)",
